    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1421">

                <pb facs="1136" n="1020" xml:id="pg1020"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.00/1761.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                        Minister.</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1421-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 31, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: For your information and with reference to
                    Mr. Gunther’s telegram of January 4th to the Department, you are advised that
                    Consul Lee, in whose custody the Legation at San José now is, reported under
                    date of January 16th that he could not, after careful investigation, verify the
                    rumor that Gámez was lending assistance to any movement against Nicaragua, or
                    that he was in constant communication with General Vásquez. He added that in San
                    José there was no evidence of the existence of any activity against
                    Nicaragua.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1421-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1421-f1-content">
                <p>The same to the American Ministers to Salvador and Guatemala.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
